{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Let the waters swarm.</b> After the luminaries were set, He created all living creatures. <b>The waters.</b> All waters, even those in vessels, swarm worms after their kind; therefore it did not write 'the waters' (הימים)." "<b>The firmament of the heavens.</b> In many places the air is called 'heavens' (שמים): 'that flies in the heavens' (שמים), 'stretch out your hand toward the heavens' (שמים), 'its head reached the heavens' (שמים), 'great and fortified cities in the heavens' (בשמים), and in the language of the Mishnah we find 'from the earth to the heavens of the rafters' (שמי קורה). And 'and it was so' (ויהי כן) was not written in the account of the fifth day, because in it the fish were created, and there was no creation visibly apparent to the eyes like the creations of the other days."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:19:34.188775146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}